          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Simple Flux 2 Klein Inpaint Workflow\n\nAuthor: Rio\n\nVersion: 1.0\n\n## Purpose: \n\nMake easier the inpainting for rookies like me.\n\n## How it Works\n\n**Image:** Upload your photo to the Load Image node.\n\n**Mask:** Paint the area you want to modify using the mask editor.\n\n**Prompt:** Enter the description of the new detail in the CLIP Text Encode node.\n\n**Generate:** Click \"Queue Prompt\" to run the inpainting process.\n\n## Required Models\n\n**Flux Model (Klein 4B):** \n[Download](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4B/resolve/main/flux-2-klein-4b.safetensors?download=true)\n \n**Text Encoder (Qwen 3 4B):** [Download](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_4b.safetensors?download=true)\n\n**Flux VAE:** [Download](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/vae-text-encorder-for-flux-klein-4b/resolve/main/split_files/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors)\n\n## Credits\n**Creator:** Workflow developed by Rio.\n\n\n**Civitai Profile:** [View Profile](https://civitai.com/user/Rio__)\n\n\n  \n\n*If you think there is anything that can be done or implemented in a better way, I would be happy to hear it because I am learning too.* "
      ],
